IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 2: s 9 (modification of licence conditions) and s 10 (suspension or cancellation of licence, etc.).
-- The seat is the licensee's: what may be done to my licence, with what notice, with what protection.
-- 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 9 was s 7, s 10 was s 8.

§ `s 9 Modification of licence conditions`

-- src:993 | 9.—(1) Subject to this section, the Authority may modify the
-- src:994 | conditions of a licence granted under section 5 or 7.
@ref s 9(1) (src:993-994)
GIVEN `the licence was granted under section 5 or 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(1): the Authority may modify the conditions of the licence` MEANS
    `the licence was granted under section 5 or 7`

-- src:998 | (2) Before making modifications to the conditions of a licence of a
-- src:999 | public telecommunication licensee under this section, the Authority
-- src:1000 | must give notice to the licensee —
-- src:1002 | (a) stating that it proposes to make the modifications in the
-- src:1003 | manner as specified in the notice and the compensation
-- src:1004 | payable for any damage caused by the modifications; and
-- src:1006 | (b) specifying the time (being at least 28 days from the date of
-- src:1007 | service of notice on the licensee) within which written
-- src:1008 | representations with respect to the proposed modifications
-- src:1009 | may be made.
@ref s 9(2) (src:998-1009)
GIVEN `the licensee is a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the Authority proposes to make the modifications in the manner specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the compensation payable for any damage caused by the modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the date of service of the notice allowed for written representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2): the notice is as the Authority must give before modifying the licence conditions` MEANS
        `the licensee is a public telecommunication licensee`
    AND `the notice states that the Authority proposes to make the modifications in the manner specified in the notice`
    AND `the notice states the compensation payable for any damage caused by the modifications`
    AND (`days from the date of service of the notice allowed for written representations` AT LEAST 28)

-- src:1014 | (3) Upon receipt of any written representation mentioned in
-- src:1015 | subsection (2), the Authority must consider the representation and
-- src:1016 | may —
-- src:1018 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:1020 | (b) amend the proposed modifications or compensation
-- src:1021 | payable in accordance with the representation, or
-- src:1022 | otherwise,
-- src:1024 | and, in either event, the Authority must issue a written direction to the
-- src:1025 | licensee requiring that effect be given to the proposed modifications
-- src:1026 | specified in the notice or to such modifications as subsequently
-- src:1027 | amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
@ref s 9(3) (src:1014-1027)
GIVEN `the Authority received a written representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority considered the representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority issued a written direction within a reasonable time requiring effect be given to the proposed modifications, or to them as amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(3): the Authority has acted as the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority received a written representation`) OR (`the Authority considered the representation` AND `the Authority issued a written direction within a reasonable time requiring effect be given to the proposed modifications, or to them as amended`)

-- src:1029 | (4) The Authority must not enforce its direction —
-- src:1031 | (a) during the period mentioned in section 89(1) or (7);
-- src:1033 | (b) while a reconsideration request of the public
-- src:1034 | telecommunication licensee under section 89 in respect
-- src:1035 | of a decision of the Authority under this section is under
-- src:1036 | consideration by the Authority; or
-- src:1038 | (c) while an appeal of the public telecommunication licensee
-- src:1039 | under section 89 in respect of a decision of the Authority
-- src:1040 | under this section is under consideration by the Minister.
@ref s 9(4) (src:1029-1040)
GIVEN `it is within the period mentioned in section 89(1) or (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reconsideration request of the public telecommunication licensee under section 89 about a decision under this section is under consideration by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal of the public telecommunication licensee under section 89 about a decision under this section is under consideration by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(4): the Authority may enforce its direction` MEANS
    NOT (   `it is within the period mentioned in section 89(1) or (7)`
         OR `a reconsideration request of the public telecommunication licensee under section 89 about a decision under this section is under consideration by the Authority`
         OR `an appeal of the public telecommunication licensee under section 89 about a decision under this section is under consideration by the Minister`)

-- src:1044 | (5) If no written representation is received by the Authority within
-- src:1045 | the time specified in subsection (2) or if any written representation
-- src:1046 | made under that subsection is subsequently withdrawn, the Authority
-- src:1047 | may forthwith carry out the modifications as specified in the notice
-- src:1048 | given under that subsection.
@ref s 9(5) (src:1044-1048)
GIVEN `no written representation was received within the time specified in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written representation made under subsection (2) was subsequently withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(5): the Authority may forthwith carry out the modifications specified in the notice` MEANS
    `no written representation was received within the time specified in subsection (2)` OR `a written representation made under subsection (2) was subsequently withdrawn`

§ `s 10(1) to (2): contravention and the Authority's powers`

-- src:1054 | 10.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that a person who is granted a
-- src:1055 | licence under section 5 or 7 or any regulations made under this Act is
-- src:1056 | contravening, or has contravened, whether by act or omission —
-- src:1058 | (a) any of the conditions of the licence or part thereof;
-- src:1060 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1061 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 22
-- src:1063 | (b) any provision of any code of practice or standard of
-- src:1064 | performance;
-- src:1066 | (c) any direction of the Authority given under section 31,
-- src:1067 | 40(2)(a), (b) or (c), 41(2)(d)(ii) or 43(3); or
-- src:1069 | (d) section 38 or any terms or conditions of participation in a
-- src:1070 | dispute resolution scheme (within the meaning of
-- src:1071 | section 51(2)),
@ref s 10(1) grounds (src:1054-1071)
GIVEN `the person is granted a licence under section 5 or 7, or is bound by regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a condition of the licence or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a provision of a code of practice or standard of performance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority given under section 31, 40(2)(a), (b) or (c), 41(2)(d)(ii) or 43(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, section 38 or a term or condition of participation in a dispute resolution scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(1): the Authority may by written notice issue an order or require a financial penalty` MEANS
        `the person is granted a licence under section 5 or 7, or is bound by regulations made under this Act`
    AND (   `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a condition of the licence or part of one`
         OR `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a provision of a code of practice or standard of performance`
         OR `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority given under section 31, 40(2)(a), (b) or (c), 41(2)(d)(ii) or 43(3)`
         OR `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, section 38 or a term or condition of participation in a dispute resolution scheme`)

-- src:1073 | the Authority may, by written notice, do either or both of the
-- src:1074 | following:
-- src:1076 | (e) issue such written order to the person as the Authority
-- src:1077 | considers requisite for the purpose of securing compliance
-- src:1078 | thereof;
-- src:1080 | (f) require the person to pay, within a specified period, a
-- src:1081 | financial penalty of an amount not exceeding the higher of
-- src:1082 | the following amounts:
-- src:1084 | (i) 10% of the annual turnover of that part of the
-- src:1085 | person’s business in respect of which the person is
-- src:1086 | granted the licence, as ascertained from the person’s
-- src:1087 | latest audited accounts;
-- src:1089 | (ii) $1 million. [10/2005; 19/2011; 30/2016]
@ref s 10(1)(e) and (f) (src:1073-1089)
GIVEN `the Authority considers the order requisite for the purpose of securing compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(1)(e): the Authority may issue this written order` MEANS
    `the Authority considers the order requisite for the purpose of securing compliance`

GIVEN `annual turnover in dollars of that part of the person's business in respect of which the person is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10(1)(f): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`annual turnover in dollars of that part of the person's business in respect of which the person is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1) GREATER THAN 1000000
           THEN `annual turnover in dollars of that part of the person's business in respect of which the person is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1
           OTHERWISE 1000000

-- src:1090 | (2) If the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:1092 | (a) the person mentioned in subsection (1) is again likely to
-- src:1093 | contravene, whether by act or omission, any condition,
-- src:1094 | provision, direction or section mentioned in that
-- src:1095 | subsection;
-- src:1097 | (b) the person mentioned in subsection (1) has gone into
-- src:1098 | liquidation other than for the purpose of amalgamation or
-- src:1099 | reconstruction;
-- src:1101 | (c) the person mentioned in subsection (1) is no longer in a
-- src:1102 | position to comply with this Act or the terms or conditions
-- src:1103 | of the person’s licence; or
-- src:1105 | (d) the public interest so requires,
-- src:1107 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1108 | 23 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1110 | the Authority may (in lieu of an order or a financial penalty under
-- src:1111 | subsection (1)(e) or (f)) by written notice and without payment of any
-- src:1112 | compensation or refund of any fee, do all or any of the following:
-- src:1114 | (e) cancel the licence or part thereof;
-- src:1116 | (f) suspend the licence or part thereof for such period as the
-- src:1117 | Authority thinks fit;
-- src:1119 | (g) reduce the period for which the licence is to be in force.
@ref s 10(2) (src:1090-1119)
GIVEN `the person is again likely to contravene a condition, provision, direction or section mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is no longer in a position to comply with this Act or the terms or conditions of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public interest so requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(2): the Authority may by written notice, without compensation or refund of any fee, cancel the licence or part, suspend it, or reduce its period` MEANS
        `the person is again likely to contravene a condition, provision, direction or section mentioned in subsection (1)`
    OR `the person has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`
    OR `the person is no longer in a position to comply with this Act or the terms or conditions of the licence`
    OR `the public interest so requires`

§ `s 10(3) to (8): the order, the offence, the penalty as a debt`

-- src:1123 | (3) An order under subsection (1)(e) —
-- src:1125 | (a) may require the person concerned (according to the
-- src:1126 | circumstances of the case) to do, or to refrain from
-- src:1127 | doing, such things as are specified in the order, or as are of
-- src:1128 | a description specified in the order; and
-- src:1130 | (b) takes effect at such time (being the earliest practicable
-- src:1131 | time) as is determined by or under that order.
@ref s 10(3) (src:1123-1131)
GIVEN `the thing is specified in the order or is of a description specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(3)(a): the order may require the person to do, or refrain from doing, the thing` MEANS
    `the thing is specified in the order or is of a description specified in the order`

GIVEN `the time is the earliest practicable time determined by or under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(3)(b): the order takes effect at this time` MEANS
    `the time is the earliest practicable time determined by or under the order`

-- src:1135 | (4) The Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:1136 | whole or any part of an order under subsection (1)(e).
@ref s 10(4) (src:1135-1136)
GIVEN `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or a part of an order under subsection (1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(4): the Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the order` MEANS
    `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or a part of an order under subsection (1)(e)`

-- src:1140 | (5) Any person who fails to comply with any order under
-- src:1141 | subsection (1)(e) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable
-- src:1142 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment
-- src:1143 | for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 10(5) (src:1140-1143)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an order under subsection (1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 10(5): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person fails to comply with an order under subsection (1)(e)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 100000, 36, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1147 | (6) In any proceedings brought against any person for an offence
-- src:1148 | under subsection (5), it is a defence for the person to prove that the
-- src:1149 | person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to
-- src:1150 | avoid contravening the order.
@ref s 10(6) (src:1147-1150)
GIVEN `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid contravening the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(6): the person has a defence to the offence under subsection (5)` MEANS
    `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid contravening the order`

-- src:1152 | (7) If the Authority, by written notice under subsection (1), requires
-- src:1153 | a person who is granted a licence to pay, within a specified period, a
-- src:1154 | financial penalty under subsection (1)(f), and the person fails or
-- src:1155 | refuses to pay the financial penalty within the specified period, the
-- src:1156 | Authority may, by written notice and without payment of any
-- src:1157 | compensation or refund of any fee, do all or any of the following:
@ref s 10(7) (src:1152-1157)
GIVEN `the Authority required the person by written notice to pay a financial penalty under subsection (1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails or refuses to pay within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(7): the Authority may by written notice, without compensation or refund of any fee, cancel the licence or part, suspend it, or reduce its period` MEANS
    `the Authority required the person by written notice to pay a financial penalty under subsection (1)(f)` AND `the person fails or refuses to pay within the specified period`

-- src:1159 | (a) cancel the licence or part thereof;
-- src:1161 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1162 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 24
-- src:1164 | (b) suspend the licence or part thereof for such period as the
-- src:1165 | Authority thinks fit;
-- src:1167 | (c) reduce the period for which the licence is to be in force.
@ref s 10(7)(a) to (c) (src:1159-1167)
GIVEN `the Authority cancels the licence or part, suspends it for such period as it thinks fit, or reduces the period for which it is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(7)(a) to (c): the Authority has taken a step open to it` MEANS
    `the Authority cancels the licence or part, suspends it for such period as it thinks fit, or reduces the period for which it is in force`

-- src:1171 | (8) Any financial penalty payable by any person under
-- src:1172 | subsection (1)(f) is recoverable by the Authority as a debt due to
-- src:1173 | the Authority from that person; and the person’s liability to pay is not
-- src:1174 | affected by the person’s licence ceasing (for any reason) to be in
-- src:1175 | force.
@ref s 10(8) (src:1171-1175)
GIVEN `the financial penalty is payable under subsection (1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has ceased to be in force for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(8): the person is liable to pay the financial penalty, recoverable by the Authority as a debt` MEANS
    `the financial penalty is payable under subsection (1)(f)`
